ms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/23d682d0-068e-4fa1-8633-8ba46a7829d8.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":51,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/ae21f6ce-2344-4a44-be18-1309cd532e16.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/90d01e73-48d2-4c32-9ce8-edf3078d6d65.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/8507617c-da78-4382-b350-fd94d283df4c.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":52,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/df089650-7f28-4317-ae7c-9c0dba8604f4.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/39629bab-2f79-483b-ab7d-c5f44740568c.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/8a0ef58b-1bd0-47a9-83ec-a7ebe347c7d6.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/99a3dc18-e820-4cb0-8096-182cae8843c3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":53,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/da2e3f9a-35c1-4513-9513-4e3129bcb8d0.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/c9e72dde-fac8-4d6b-bd9e-52deb8372ce4.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":54,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/9cd0736d-4254-40ba-8964-8582afe3b95c.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><span>Answer: (c)<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span>Solution:<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span><strong>Grammar 1:</strong> Not LL (1) due to Left Recursion and Ambiguity.</span><o:p></o:p></p>\n<p><o:p> </o:p></p>\n<p><span><strong>Grammar 2:</strong> Not LL (1) due to Left Recursion.</span><o:p></o:p></p>\n<p></p>\n<p><span>Ambiguity (Dangling Else): The production E&rarr;if E then E else E still contains the dangling-else ambiguity from Grammar 1. An ambiguous grammar cannot be LL(1) or even LALR(1) in a deterministic parser.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span>LL(1) Check (FIRST/FOLLOW): Let's assume we fix the ambiguity or ignore it for the FIRST/FOLLOW test:<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span>FIRST(&alpha;1)=FIRST(if E then E else E)={if}<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span><span>FIRST(&alpha;2</span><span>​</span><span> )=FIRST(do E then E)={do}<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>FIRST(&alpha;3</span><span>​</span><span>)=FIRST(id)={id}<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>Since {if}&cap;{do}=</span><span>&empty;</span><span>, {if}</span><span>&cap;</span><span>{id}=</span><span>&empty;</span><span>, and {do}</span><span>&cap;</span><span>{id}=</span><span>&empty;</span><span>, this grammar satisfies the FIRST-set condition for non-left-recursive productions.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p></p>\n<p><span>Consider FIRST sets:<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><span>FIRST(if E then E else E) = { if }<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><span>FIRST(do E then E) = { do }<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><span>FIRST(id) = { id }<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span>All FIRST sets are <strong>distinct</strong>, and:<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><span>No left recursion<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><span>No &epsilon;-productions<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><span>No FIRST&ndash;FIRST or FIRST&ndash;FOLLOW conflicts<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p></p>\n<p><span><span>Therefore, <strong>Grammar 3 IS LL(1)</strong>.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":55,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/071004b3-32e2-431e-a2c3-f37ac143a579.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/c687cce8-2091-49a2-ad45-1aba076793f7.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":56,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/e140288f-60a5-48ce-8e70-b1b1bf29cb99.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{